       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, and I shouldn't have offered to earlier. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is three times the maximum dose. It has no therapeutic benefit over 2,550 mg/day and carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function. I don't want to put in an order that could seriously harm your patient, even with your confirmation.\n\nIf I've misread the intent, I can enter any of these right away:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- A lower or titrated dose, such as 500 mg twice daily with meals\n- Another dose you specify that is within the labeled maximum\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for this dose, such as a toxicology or protocol-driven situation, please talk to your attending and pharmacy. They can enter it through a pathway with the appropriate verification."
